            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "In $(F,E,V)$ order: triangular $(4,6,4)$; rectangular $(5,8,5)$; pentagonal $(6,10,6)$; hexagonal $(7,12,7)$.",
              "worked": "An $n$-sided pyramid has $n$ triangular faces and one base, $n$ base edges and $n$ edges to the apex, and $n$ base vertices plus the apex. Thus $F=n+1$, $E=2n$ and $V=n+1$. For $n=3,4,5,6$, the counts $(F,E,V)$ are $(4,6,4),(5,8,5),(6,10,6),(7,12,7)$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 0,
            "responseSpace": "scaffold"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "For each of the above evaluate $V-E+F$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2$ for each pyramid.",
          "worked": "Triangular: $4-6+4=2$.\n\nRectangular: $5-8+5=2$.\n\nPentagonal: $6-10+6=2$.\n\nHexagonal: $7-12+7=2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q5-c",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "If the polygonal base has $n$ sides, find in terms of $n$:",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p6-q5-c-i",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": "the number of faces $(F)$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$n+1$",
              "worked": "There are $n$ triangular side faces and one base, so $F=n+1$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 10
          },
          {
            "id": "p6-q5-c-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "the number of edges $(E)$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$2n$",
              "worked": "There are $n$ base edges and $n$ edges joining the base vertices to the apex, so $E=n+n=2n$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 10
          },
          {
            "id": "p6-q5-c-iii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "iii",
            "prompt": "the number of vertices $(V)$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$n+1$",
              "worked": "There are $n$ base vertices and one apex, so $V=n+1$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 10
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q5-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Find $V-E+F$ using the results of parts c(i), c(ii) and c(iii).",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2$",
          "worked": "$\\begin{align*}V-E+F&=(n+1)-2n+(n+1)\\\\V-E+F&=2.\\end{align*}$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      }
    ]
